event: delegated_tool_call
data: {"agent":"coordinator","agent_tab":"coordinator","event":{"tool_input":{"content":"# Daily Self-Evolution Monitor — Day 01\n**Task Family:** `optimization_probe`\n**Date:** 2026-05-25\n**Predecessor Artifacts:**\n- `self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_precipitation_seed.md` — stable refs R1–R9, bounded counters C1–C25\n- `self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_reuse_followup.md` — per-skill visibility, 19.3/100 precipitation score\n- `self_evolution_optimization_metrics_probe_28.md` — 8 of 11 optimization metrics absent\n- `self_evolution_closed_loop_metric_contract_probe_29.md` — Contract C1 unfilled, P1 satisfied, P2–P5 fail\n- `self_evolution_reusability_probe_32.md` — zero reuse across 2,382 proposals\n- `self_evolution_agent_skill_precipitation_checklist.md` — 8-phase precipitation framework\n**Method:** Telemetry-oriented criteria audit across all 26 visible skills. Bounded inspection only. Application-neutral. No mutations.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Telemetry-Oriented Review Criteria\n\nOptimization in a self-evolving system requires a closed-loop substrate:\n\n```\nObservation (metric capture) → Analysis (delta detection) → Intervention (optimized procedure) → Re-observation (metric re-capture)\n```\n\nEach skill in the workspace is assessed against **6 telemetry-oriented criteria** that must be present for any improvement to be measurable:\n\n| Criterion | ID | Definition | Evidence Path |\n|-----------|----|------------|--------------|\n| **Invocation Tracking** | `T1` | Per-skill count of how many times the skill was invoked | `_usage.json` → `invocationCount` field, or `activation_count` in telemetry aggregate |\n| **Duration Baseline** | `T2` | Execution duration captured before and after an intervention | `agent-replay-*.jsonl` → `duration_ms` field, or `completedSummary` with timing data |\n| **Failure Rate** | `T3` | Retry count and failure reason per skill invocation | `last-tool-error.json` with `retry_count` + `skill_id` cross-ref, or per-invocation error log |\n| **Tool/Token Cost** | `T4` | Tool-call count or token totals per invocation (input/output) | OMC schema → `tool_call_count` or `token_usage` fields; replay log enrichment |\n| **Activation Reach** | `T5` | Number of distinct execution cycles or agent sessions that triggered the skill | Registry entries, MCP server registrations, `.registry.json` with cross-session refs |\n| **Before/After Delta** | `T6` | Comparable baseline pair (same skill, different versions or configurations) | Paired session UUIDs, replay log timestamps, `completedSummary` version field |\n\n**Pass threshold for proposing an optimization:** A skill must satisfy **≥3 of 6 criteria** with non-zero, non-null evidence. Zero or absent on ≥4 criteria → no-change decision.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Skill-by-Skill Telemetry Criteria Assessment\n\n### 2.1 Pre-Installed Convention-Compliant Skills (4)\n\nThese skills have `SKILL.md` + valid `_meta.json` — the only skills that pass Phase 3 materialization checks.\n\n#### `playwright_mcp` (slug: `playwright-mcp`, version: `1.0.0`)\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1` Invocation Tracking | No `_usage.json` file. Zero `invocationCount` anywhere. No `.registry.json` entry. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T2` Duration Baseline | No agent-replay events reference this skill. Zero replay lines with `agent_type` matching slug. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T3` Failure Rate | No per-skill error tracking. `last-tool-error.json` contains 2 generic tool errors (Apr 28, May 4) — no skill ID cross-reference. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T4` Tool/Token Cost | OMC session schema lacks `tool_call_count` and `token_usage` fields entirely. 137 session UUID files are metadata-only. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T5` Activation Reach | MCP server config: `bing-search` only (stdio, `agent_session` lifecycle). Not skill-derived. No MCP registration for `playwright_mcp`. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T6` Before/After Delta | No before baseline exists. No `completedSummary` on any agent (all 5 agents `cs: null`). No paired session UUIDs. | **ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY (telemetry substrate absent).**\n\n#### `crypto_market` (slug: `crypto`, version: `1.0.6`)\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Identical evidence landscape to `playwright_mcp`. Zero telemetry files, zero replay cross-refs, zero registry entries, zero MCP registrations, zero before/after baselines. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n#### `stock_analysis` (slug: `stock-analysis`, version: `6.2.0`)\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Identical absence. Despite being the most content-rich skill (14,708-byte `App-Plan.md`, 8,230-byte `SKILL.md`, 12,848-byte `TODO.md`), no telemetry substrate captures its execution. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n#### `weather` (slug: `weather`, version: `1.0.0`)\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Identical absence. Smallest skill (1,169-byte `SKILL.md`, 126-byte `_meta.json`). No telemetry, no activation, no before/after. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n### 2.2 Pre-Installed Skills Without `_meta.json` (11)\n\n`chronicle`, `figma`, `figma_mcp`, `gitnexus_cli`, `gitnexus_debugging`, `gitnexus_exploring`, `gitnexus_guide`, `gitnexus_impact_analysis`, `gitnexus_pr_review`, `gitnexus_refactoring`, `golang`, `openspec`, `shadcn_ui`\n\n| Criterion | Aggregate Assessment | Verdict |\n|-----------|---------------------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | All 13 skills share the identical evidence vacuum: no `_usage.json`, no `.registry.json`, no replay cross-refs, no token/tool tracking, no MCP registration, no before/after deltas. Additionally, these skills lack `_meta.json` entirely — no versioning, no ownership, no publish timestamp to build a version-delta baseline on. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Aggregate score: 0/6 per skill. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n### 2.3 Pipeline-Produced Meta-Skills (4)\n\nThese skills describe procedures for telemetry, optimization, materialization, activation, and registry — but the infrastructure they describe does not exist.\n\n#### `telemetry_optimization`\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1` Invocation Tracking | No `_usage.json`. The skill *describes* telemetry procedures but has zero telemetry applied to itself. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T2` Duration Baseline | SKILL.md procedure: \"Use linked event-log and Agent Execution trace refs.\" Those refs exist (3 replay files) but contain no trace matching this skill. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T3` Failure Rate | No error tracking infrastructure exists for any pipeline-produced skill. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T4` Tool/Token Cost | Zero tool-call or token counters across the entire workspace. The skill's procedure template references \"event-log and Agent Execution trace refs\" — these refs do not contain cost data. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T5` Activation Reach | Not registered in any MCP config, no `.registry.json`, no load-path. The skill's own description references \"registry visibility\" — no registry exists. | **ABSENT** |\n| `T6` Before/After Delta | The skill was created once (attested by 1 mutation memento at `2026-05-25T15:12:17Z`). No version updates, no before/after pair, no `completedSummary` transition. | **ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY (self-referential meta-skill without substrate).**\n\n#### `materialization_activation_telemetry_registry`\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | The SKILL.md procedure string differs from `telemetry_optimization` only by keyword substitution (`\"telemetry, optimization\"` → `\"materialization, activation, telemetry, registry\"`). The substrate is identical: zero files, zero counters, zero activation. The skill name references infrastructure components that all return empty or 404 when probed (no materialization pipeline, no activation mechanism, no registry, no SSE signals). | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY (self-referential meta-skill describing absent infrastructure).**\n\n#### `materialization_proposal_linked_skill_package_registry_load_path`\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Same template structure. The skill references \"registry-load-path\" — no load-path configuration exists anywhere in the workspace. SKILL.md contains no concrete commands, no code blocks, no executable steps. Mutation memento attests creation only. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n#### `materialization_skill_package_registry_load_path_usage_telemetry`\n\n| Criterion | Evidence | Verdict |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Same template. This skill's name literally includes \"usage-telemetry\" — yet no `_usage.json` file exists for it or any other skill. The skill describes what it lacks. | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Score: 0/6. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY.**\n\n### 2.4 Pipeline-Produced Experimental Skills (5)\n\n`skill-exp-052e6a93-...`, `skill-exp-2b07b1df-...`, `skill-exp-4d613241-...`, `skill_exp_0bd3b7f3_...`, `skill_exp_1590b4d7_...`\n\n| Criterion | Aggregate Assessment | Verdict |\n|-----------|---------------------|---------|\n| `T1`–`T6` | Minimal observational snapshots. SKILL.md contents are 1–2 sentences of generic terminal-task capture evidence (output_chars, artifact_count, token_total). No concrete commands, no trigger conditions, no error handling. No `_meta.json`, no `_usage.json`, no replay cross-refs. Mutation mementos attest creation only (all `mutation_kind: \"CreateSkill\"`). | **ALL ABSENT** |\n\n**Aggregate score: 0/6 per skill. Classification: NO-OPPORTUNITY (observational snapshots, not reusable procedures).**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Telemetry Infrastructure Audit — The Root Cause\n\nAll 26 skills score **0/6** on telemetry-oriented criteria. The common root cause is the **complete absence of telemetry infrastructure** at three layers:\n\n### Layer 1 — Per-Skill Usage Tracking (would satisfy T1, T5)\n\n| Required Artifact | Actual State | Gap |\n|-------------------|-------------|-----|\n| `_usage.json` with `invocationCount`, `lastInvokedAt`, `consumedBy` | **0 files** across entire workspace | No per-skill invocation tracking |\n| `.registry.json` enumerating skill slugs with timestamps | **0 files** | No discoverable skill index |\n| `*.sse` signal files for real-time invocation events | **0 files** | No event-driven infrastructure |\n| Agent `completedSummary` non-null referencing a skill slug | **0 of 5 agents** (Contract C1 unfilled) | No pipeline completion signal |\n| MCP server registration for skill-derived endpoints | **0 servers** (only 1 pre-installed: `bing-search`) | No runtime activation |\n\n### Layer 2 — Execution Cost Tracking (would satisfy T3, T4)\n\n| Required Artifact | Actual State | Gap |\n|-------------------|-------------|-----|\n| Per-invocation `duration_ms` in replay logs keyed to skill slugs | 3 replay files, 10 events, 5 durations — all `agent_type:\"Explore\"`, no skill slug | No skill-level duration tracking |\n| `tool_call_count` per OMC session | Field absent from all 137+92=229 session UUID schemas | Schema gap |\n| `token_usage` (input/output/prompt/completion) per session | Field absent from all session schemas (`grep -r \"token\" shared/.omc/sessions/` → 0 hits) | Schema gap |\n| Per-skill `retry_count` and `failure_reason` in `last-tool-error.json` | 2 generic tool errors only (no skill ID cross-ref) | No skill-level error attribution |\n| Provider failure / recovery event log | 0 entries (all 3 MCP servers `state:Ready, failure_reason: null`) | No provider-layer telemetry |\n\n### Layer 3 — Baseline / Delta Infrastructure (would satisfy T2, T6)\n\n| Required Artifact | Actual State | Gap |\n|-------------------|-------------|-----|\n| Non-null `completedSummary` with version/iteration data | All 5 agents `cs: null` since Apr 13 2026 (43+ days) | No pipeline completion record |\n| Agent replay events with `agent_type` matching a materialized skill slug | 0 events across 3 files | No pipeline agent traces |\n| Skill version history (`version` field transitions in `_meta.json`) | 4 skills have version fields but zero have ever been updated | No version-delta baselines |\n| Before/after execution pair sharing a skill slug with different parameters | 0 pairs | No comparative measurement possible |\n| Elapsed execution time per probe or per skill invocation | Only filesystem mtime proxies exist (not service-owned) | No temporal baseline |\n\n**Root cause summary:** The telemetry substrate that would make optimization measurable does not exist. All 26 skills, regardless of origin (pre-installed vs. pipeline-produced), content depth (1,169-byte `weather` vs. 14,708-byte `stock_analysis`), or convention compliance (4 with `_meta.json` vs. 22 without), inhabit the same telemetry vacuum.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Optimization Opportunity Scan\n\nDespite the substrate absence, three structural patterns were identified that *would* become optimization opportunities once telemetry infrastructure is deployed:\n\n### 4.1 Potential Optimization A — Skill Content Duplication (Pre-Install vs. Pipeline)\n\n**Observation:** The 4 `materialization_*` meta-skills have SKILL.md content that is structurally identical to the 5 `skill-exp*` observational snapshots — same template sections (name → description → When To Use → Procedure → Verification → Provenance), same generic language, same absence of concrete commands. This is a **content duplication pattern without functional differentiation**.\n\n**Telemetry needed to convert to an optimization:** Compare `T1`/`T5` activation rates between duplicate-content skills once tracking exists. If both are invoked for the same task, one is redundant. Optimization: merge, deduplicate, or deprecate the lower-used variant.\n\n**Current verdict:** `POTENTIAL` — cannot be measured until T1/T5 infrastructure exists.\n\n### 4.2 Potential Optimization B — Convention Compliance Gap as Quality Signal\n\n**Observation:** 22 of 26 skills (85%) lack `_meta.json`. Of the 4 that have it, none carry a `proposal_id` field linking to pipeline provenance. This means zero skills carry machine-readable lifecycle metadata. Any skill could be invoked without version checking, ownership verification, or deprecation detection.\n\n**Telemetry needed to convert to an optimization:** Deploy a convention compliance checker that measures `%_meta_covered` per execution cycle. Once `_meta.json` coverage reaches a threshold (e.g., >50%), measure whether skills with metadata show higher `T1` invocation success or lower `T3` failure rates.\n\n**Current verdict:** `POTENTIAL` — intervention (convention enforcement) possible but effect unmeasurable without T1/T3 infrastructure.\n\n### 4.3 Potential Optimization C — Meta-Skill Self-Referential Loop Detection\n\n**Observation:** The 4 pipeline-produced meta-skills describe procedures for telemetry, optimization, materialization, activation, and registry — but reference only their own creation mementos and template strings. They form a **closed self-referential loop**: a skill about telemetry that has no telemetry applied to itself; a skill about optimization that has never been optimized; a skill about activation that has never been activated.\n\n**Telemetry needed to convert to an optimization:** Compare the `T5` activation reach of meta-skills vs. concrete skills. If meta-skills show zero activation after N cycles, flag as self-referential noise and propose removal or consolidation.\n\n**Current verdict:** `POTENTIAL` — pattern identified but cannot be actioned without T5 infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Governed No-Change Decision\n\n### 5.1 Decision Header\n\n```\nDECISION RECORD\n===============\nDecision ID:       opt-probe-2026-05-25-001\nDate:              2026-05-25\nTask Family:       optimization_probe (Day 01)\nReviewer:          coordinator (self-evolution monitor)\nClassification:    NO-CHANGE — governed deferral\nRationale:         All 26 skills score 0/6 on telemetry-oriented criteria\n                   (T1–T6). The telemetry substrate required to measure\n                   improvement (per-skill usage tracking, execution cost\n                   tracking, baseline/delta infrastructure) is entirely\n                   absent across all three layers. No optimization can be\n                   proposed, tested, or verified until at minimum Layer 1\n                   (per-skill usage tracking) is deployed.\n```\n\n### 5.2 Missing Metrics Register\n\nThe following metrics are **required before any optimization can be proposed** but are entirely absent:\n\n| Metric ID | Metric Name | Required For | Current Status | Deployment Priority |\n|-----------|------------|--------------|----------------|---------------------|\n| `M1` | Per-skill `invocationCount` | T1 — measuring whether a skill is used enough to optimize | Absent — no `_usage.json` exists for any skill | **P0** (gate for all other metrics) |\n| `M2` | Per-skill `lastInvokedAt` timestamp | T1, T5 — measuring recency and activation decay | Absent | P0 |\n| `M3` | Skill-to-session cross-reference in replay logs | T2, T6 — linking execution duration to specific skill usage | Absent — replay logs have `agent_type:\"Explore\"` only | P1 |\n| `M4` | Per-skill `retry_count` in error logs | T3 — measuring failure rate per skill | Absent — `last-tool-error.json` lacks skill ID field | P1 |\n| `M5` | `tool_call_count` per session | T4 — measuring automation depth | Schema absent from OMC sessions | P1 |\n| `M6` | `token_usage` per session (input + output) | T4 — measuring computational cost | Schema absent from OMC sessions | P1 |\n| `M7` | Non-null `completedSummary` on any agent | T6 — establishing the first before/after baseline pair | Absent — Contract C1 unfilled since Run 0 (51+ runs, 43+ days) | **P0** (oldest unfilled atomic repair) |\n| `M8` | `.registry.json` with skill slug enumeration | T5 — enabling skill discovery and activation reach | Absent — 0 files | P1 |\n| `M9` | Skill-level provider failure / recovery log | T3 — distinguishing skill errors from provider errors | Absent — only generic tool errors recorded | P2 |\n| `M10` | `_usage.json` `consumedBy` field listing consuming sessions | T5, T6 — establishing cross-session reuse chains | Absent — 0 files | P2 |\n\n**Condition for re-evaluation:** When ≥4 of the P0/P1 metrics (M1–M8) are populated with non-null, non-zero data, this probe should be re-executed. Until then, all optimization proposals are deferred.\n\n### 5.3 Rollback Fields\n\nSince this is a **no-change decision** (no optimization was proposed or applied), the rollback plan is procedural rather than operational:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Applied change** | None (read-only probe) |\n| **Rollback trigger** | N/A — no change to roll back |\n| **Rollback procedure** | No action needed. Previous governance artifacts (precipitation_seed, reuse_followup) provide the pre-probe baseline. |\n| **Rollback verification** | Compare C1–C25 counters between this artifact and the reuse_followup baseline. Any deviation in immutable counters (C4, C5, C8–C25) indicates unintended mutation. |\n| **Deprecation path** | If a future optimization IS proposed and later rolled back, reference this decision as the pre-optimization baseline (Decision ID `opt-probe-2026-05-25-001`). The rollback would restore to the state documented here. |\n| **Re-evaluation schedule** | Re-run this probe whenever P0 metrics (M1, M7) become non-null. The probe procedure in §9 is idempotent and can be executed on any schedule. |\n\n### 5.4 Audit Refs\n\n| Ref | Source | Content |\n|-----|--------|---------|\n| `AR1` | This artifact (§2) | Per-skill telemetry criteria assessment — all 26 skills scored 0/6 |\n| `AR2` | This artifact (§3) | Three-layer telemetry infrastructure audit — root cause analysis |\n| `AR3` | This artifact (§4) | Three potential optimizations identified but blocked by missing metrics |\n| `AR4` | This artifact (§5.2) | Missing Metrics Register — 10 required metrics (M1–M10) |\n| `AR5` | `reuse_followup.md` §3.1 | C1–C25 counter deltas — baseline for this probe |\n| `AR6` | `precipitation_seed.md` §2 | Stable refs R1–R9 — canonical data sources |\n| `AR7` | `optimization_metrics_probe_28.md` §2 | 8 of 11 optimization metrics absent (predecessor finding) |\n| `AR8` | `closed_loop_metric_contract_probe_29.md` §5 | Contract C1 unfilled — P0 atomic repair |\n| `AR9` | `agent_skill_precipitation_checklist.md` §7 | Precipitation scoring framework — all skills score ≤19.3/100 |\n| `AR10` | Mutation mementos (17 files) | All `mutation_kind: \"CreateSkill\"` — zero activation/reuse events attested |\n\n**Chain of custody:** This artifact is a read-only probe. It appends to the governance chain (R3) without modifying any other ref. All evidence is bounded to the stable refs enumerated in the precipitation seed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Counter Snapshot (Day 01, optimization_probe)\n\n| ID | Counter | Value | Δ from reuse_followup | Signal |\n|----|---------|-------|----------------------|--------|\n| `C1` | Governance artifacts | **56** | +1 | 📈 Monotonic governance growth |\n| `C2` | Governance lines | **12,746** | +332 | 📈 Probe documentation |\n| `C3` | Verification artifacts | 6 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C4` | `available_skills/` dirs | 26 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C5` | Convention-compliant dirs | 4 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C6` | Pipeline-produced (proposal_id) | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C7` | `_meta.json` with `proposal_id` | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C8` | Agent replay files | 3 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C9` | Replay events | 10 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C10` | Duration captures | 5 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C11` | Missions | 3 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C12` | Agents | 5 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C13` | Non-null `completedSummary` | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C14` | `.registry.json` files | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C15` | `_usage.json` files | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C16` | `*.sse` files | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C17` | MCP servers (pre-installed) | 1 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C18` | MCP servers (proposal-derived) | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C19` | Skill catalog entries (ops API) | 4 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C20` | Curation/rejection/promotion artifacts | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C21` | Session UUIDs (shared) | 137 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C22` | Session UUIDs (root) | 92 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C23` | Source-root skill packages | 5 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C24` | Mutation mementos | 17 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n| `C25` | Crontab entries | 0 | 0 | ✅ Stable |\n\n**All immutable counters Δ=0. Only C1 (+1 artifact) and C2 (+332 lines) grew — monotonic governance growth.**\n\n---\n\n## 7. Invariant Assertions (All Hold)\n\n```python\n# I1: All agents have completedSummary = null\n# I2: Zero telemetry infrastructure (_usage.json, .registry.json, *.sse)\n# I3: No pipeline-produced skills with proposal_id in _meta.json\n# I4: No registry/load-path/SSE infrastructure\n# I5: No crontab entries\n# I6: MCP count stable (1 pre-installed server)\n# I7: All 26 skills score 0/6 on telemetry criteria\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Conclusions\n\n### 8.1 No Optimization Is Currently Provable\n\n**After reviewing all 26 skills across 6 telemetry-oriented criteria (T1–T6):**\n- **0 of 26 skills** satisfy even 1 criterion with non-null evidence\n- **All 26 skills** score **0/6**\n- **10 required metrics** (M1–M10) are entirely absent\n- **3 potential optimizations** identified (content deduplication, convention gap meta-skill, self-referential loop detection) — all blocked by missing telemetry infrastructure\n- **Contract C1** (non-null `completedSummary`) remains unfilled after 51+ runs, 43+ days\n\n### 8.2 Classification\n\n```\nOptimization status:    NOT-PROVABLE\nDecision type:          GOVERNED NO-CHANGE (deferral)\nTelemetry coverage:     0/6 criteria met across all 26 skills\nMissing metrics:        10 (M1–M10), 4 at P0 priority\nPotential optimizations: 3 identified but blocked\nBlocking gate:         Layer 1 telemetry infrastructure deployment\n                       (per-skill usage tracking: _usage.json + invocationCount)\nRe-evaluation trigger:  When ≥4 P0/P1 metrics (M1–M8) become non-null\n```\n\n### 8.3 What Would Change This Classification\n\nThe following single atomic intervention would change the classification from NO-CHANGE to PROVISIONAL-OPPORTUNITY:\n\n1. **Deploy per-skill `_usage.json`** with at minimum `invocationCount`, `lastInvokedAt`, and `consumedBy` fields (M1, M2, M10).\n2. **Write a non-null `completedSummary`** on any agent referencing a skill slug (M7 — Contract C1 from Run 22).\n3. **Re-run this probe** — any skill with `invocationCount ≥ 1` would satisfy T1, qualifying for provisional optimization assessment.\n\n**This is the same atomic repair first identified in Run 22 (§7) and unfilled through 29 subsequent runs.**\n\n---\n\n## 9. Reusable Probe Procedure\n\nApplication-neutral. No business logic, provider names, raw prompts, or secrets. Idempotent — produces only this governance artifact.\n\n### Phase 1 — Telemetry Infrastructure Scan\n\n```bash\n# === Check per-skill usage tracking (T1) ===\nfind . -name \"_usage.json\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" -not -path \"*/.next/*\" | wc -l\n\n# === Check skill registry (T5) ===\nfind . -name \".registry.json\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" -not -path \"*/.next/*\" | wc -l\nfind . -name \"*.sse\" -not -path \"*/node_modules/*\" -not -path \"*/.next/*\" | wc -l\n\n# === Check execution cost tracking (T3, T4) ===\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\n# Check OMC session schema for tool_call_count / token fields\nimport glob\nsessions = glob.glob('shared/.omc/sessions/*.json') + glob.glob('.omc/sessions/*.json')\nhas_tool_count = has_token = False\nfor f in sessions[:10]:\n    try:\n        d = json.load(open(f))\n        if 'tool_call_count' in d or 'tool_invocations' in d: has_tool_count = True\n        if any(k in d for k in ['token_usage','input_tokens','output_tokens','total_tokens']): has_token = True\n    except: pass\nprint(f'tool_call_count field present: {has_tool_count}')\nprint(f'token_usage field present: {has_token}')\n\"\n\n# === Check baseline infrastructure (T2, T6) ===\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nms = json.load(open('shared/.omc/state/mission-state.json'))\nnon_null = [a.get('completedSummary') for m in ms['missions'] for a in m['agents'] if a.get('completedSummary') is not None]\nprint(f'Non-null completedSummary count: {len(non_null)}')\nif non_null:\n    print(f'Values: {non_null}')\n\"\n```\n\n### Phase 2 — Per-Skill Telemetry Criteria Scoring\n\n```bash\n# For each skill in available_skills/*/, score T1–T6\nfor d in available_skills/*/; do\n  name=$(basename \"$d\")\n  score=0\n  [ -f \"$d/_usage.json\" ] && score=$((score + 1))\n  [ -f \"$d/../.registry.json\" ] || [ -f \".registry.json\" ] && score=$((score + 1))\n  python3 -c \"\nimport json\nms = json.load(open('shared/.omc/state/mission-state.json'))\nrefs = [a.get('completedSummary') for m in ms['missions'] for a in m['agents'] if a.get('completedSummary') == '$name']\nprint(len(refs))\n\" 2>/dev/null | grep -q '^[1-9]' && score=$((score + 1))\n  echo \"$name: $score/6\"\ndone\n```\n\n### Phase 3 — Before/After Delta Detection\n\n```bash\n# Compare current counters with previous snapshot\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\ntry:\n    prev = json.load(open('/tmp/optimization_probe_snapshot_before.json'))\n    # Re-capture current counters and diff\n    print('Delta comparison available if before-snapshot exists')\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print('No before-snapshot found. Run Phase 4 first to establish baseline.')\n\"\n```\n\n### Phase 4 — Snapshot Capture (for future delta)\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"\nimport json, glob, subprocess\nsnap = {}\nsnap['C1'] = len(glob.glob('shared/self_evolution_*.md'))\nsnap['C4'] = len(glob.glob('available_skills/*/'))\nsnap['C5'] = sum(1 for d in glob.glob('available_skills/*/') if glob.glob(d+'SKILL.md') and glob.glob(d+'_meta.json'))\nsnap['C8'] = len(glob.glob('shared/.omc/state/agent-replay-*.jsonl'))\nsnap['C13'] = subprocess.run(['python3','-c','import json;ms=json.load(open(\\\"shared/.omc/state/mission-state.json\\\"));print(sum(1 for m in ms[\\\"missions\\\"] for a in m[\\\"agents\\\"] if a.get(\\\"completedSummary\\\") is not None))'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip()\nsnap['C14'] = len(subprocess.run(['find','.','-name','.registry.json'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip().split(chr(10))) - 1\nsnap['C15'] = len(subprocess.run(['find','.','-name','_usage.json'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout.strip().split(chr(10))) - 1\nwith open('/tmp/optimization_probe_snapshot_before.json','w') as f:\n    json.dump(snap, f, indent=2)\nprint('Before snapshot saved to /tmp/optimization_probe_snapshot_before.json')\n\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 10. Artifact Management\n\n| Rule | Value |\n|------|-------|\n| **Artifact name** | `shared/self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_optimization_probe.md` |\n| **Growth (C1/C2)** | Monotonic: 56 artifacts, 12,746 lines |\n| **Mutation** | Zero files created/modified outside this governance artifact ✅ |\n| **Retention** | Predecessor artifacts preserved (48→55→56 chain) ✅ |\n| **Rollback** | No change to roll back. Previous snapshot at `reuse_followup.md` §3.1 provides pre-probe baseline. |\n| **Re-execution** | Procedure in §9 is idempotent. Re-run when P0 metrics (M1, M7) become non-null. |\n| **Naming convention** | `shared/self_evolution_YYYY-MM-DD_day-NN_<task_family>.md` |\n\n---\n\n*End of Day 01 optimization_probe. Application-neutral. No business logic, provider names, raw prompts, secrets, or unbounded output captured. All 26 skills scored 0/6 on telemetry-oriented criteria (T1–T6). No-change decision with governed deferral. 10 missing metrics (M1–M10) registered. 3 potential optimizations identified but blocked by missing substrate. Contract C1 remains the P0 atomic repair (unfilled since Run 22, 29+ subsequent runs). Stable refs R1–R9. Bounded counters C1–C25 with deltas. Rollback fields and audit refs (AR1–AR10) documented.*\n","path":"shared/self_evolution_2026-05-25_day-01_optimization_probe.md"},"tool_name":"file_write","type":"tool_call"},"task_id":"39e8b501-5d94-42e2-918f-cb7afedce4a2"}

